## Suggested Tour Routes in Cairo

| Day | Route | Highlights | Practical Tips |
|-----|-------|------------|----------------|
| **Day 1 – Ancient Wonders** | 1️⃣ Giza Pyramid Complex (Great Pyramid, Khafre, Menkaure, Sphinx) <br>2️⃣ Solar Boat Museum <br>3️⃣ Optional: Al‑Giza Zoo | • The iconic pyramids and the Sphinx <br>• Ancient solar boat replica <br>• Small zoo with local fauna | • Arrive early (8 am) to avoid crowds & heat <br>• Wear comfortable shoes, bring water & sunscreen <br>• Entrance fees: ~30 E£ (pyramids), ~10 E£ (boat museum) |
| **Day 2 – Cairo’s Cultural Core** | 1️⃣ Egyptian Museum (Tahrir Square) <br>2️⃣ Coptic Cairo (Hanging Church, Ben Ezra Synagogue, Coptic Museum) <br>3️⃣ Khan el‑Khalili Bazaar <br>4️⃣ Optional: Al‑Azhar Mosque | • 120,000+ artifacts, Tutankhamun treasures <br>• 4th‑century churches & synagogue <br>• Traditional market & street food <br>• Historic mosque & university | • Museum open 9 am–5 pm (closed Fridays) <br>• Bazaar open 9 am–9 pm, free entry <br>• Entrance fees: ~30 E£ (museum), ~10 E£ (Coptic Museum) |
| **Day 3 – Modern Cairo & Views** | 1️⃣ Cairo Tower <br>2️⃣ Al‑Maamoura Mosque <br>3️⃣ Al‑Zaytuna Mosque <br>4️⃣ Al‑Hussein Mosque <br>5️⃣ Al‑Mokattam Hill (sunset walk) <br>6️⃣ Optional: Nile River Cruise (evening) | • Panoramic city view <br>• Historic mosques & library <br>• Sunset over the city <br>• Dinner & live music on the Nile | • Tower open 9 am–9 pm, entrance ~20 E£ <br>• Mosques open 9 am–5 pm, entrance ~5 E£ <br>• Cruise departs 7 pm, price ~200 E£ (incl. dinner) |

### How to Use This Itinerary

1. **Book tickets in advance** where possible (especially for the pyramids and the Egyptian Museum).  
2. **Plan your transport** – Cairo’s traffic can be heavy; consider using a reputable taxi app or a private driver for the Giza day.  
3. **Stay hydrated** – the heat can be intense, especially in the Giza area.  
4. **Dress modestly** when visiting mosques (cover shoulders & knees).  
5. **Try local cuisine** – koshary, falafel, and street‑food stalls in Khan el‑Khalili are a must‑taste.

